    "body": "As for naming,\n\n> Although the proposed name has \"hint\" in the name, the explainer at least seems to make normative requirements about behavior. That seems wrong, especially for something that cannot be directly observed.\n\nThis sounds reasonable. I prefer keeping this a hint, i.e. weak +1 for azaika@'s latter proposal:\n\n> we could consider a name that discourages caching for one-off scripts (like \"unwilling\" or \"ephemeral\") rather than strictly prohibiting it.\n\nbecause I don't think we have reasons/motivation to introduce and maintain the \"must-not-cache\" normative semantics right now.",
